00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:29,076
Some Live to Climb. They Climb to Live.

2
00:14:46,153 --> 00:14:52,153
Sherpa is a documentary film directed by Jennifer Peedom.

3
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:15,230
In 2013, the world's media reported on a shocking mountain-high
brawl as European climbers fled a mob of angry Sherpas.

4
00:29:32,307 --> 00:29:38,307
Director Jennifer Peedom and her team set out to uncover the cause of this altercation,
intending to film the 2014 climbing season from the Sherpa's point-of-view.

5
00:36:55,384 --> 00:37:01,384
Instead, they captured Everest's greatest tragedy, when a huge
block of ice crashed down onto the climbing route...

6
00:44:18,461 --> 00:44:24,461
Self, played by Russell Brice.

7
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:47,538
Self, played by Tim Medvetz.

8
00:59:04,615 --> 00:59:10,615
Self, played by Pasang Tenzing Sherpa.

9
01:06:27,692 --> 01:06:33,692
Self, played by Phurba Tashi Sherpa.

10
01:13:50,769 --> 01:13:56,769
Sherpa is a 2015 documentary film by Australian filmmaker Jennifer Peedom.

11
01:21:13,846 --> 01:21:19,846
It was filmed during the 2014 Mount Everest ice avalanche.

12
01:28:36,923 --> 01:28:42,923
The film explores themes of nepal, natural disaster,
native peoples, woman director, mount everest.
